      "text_raw": "Digital transitions of the\ndigital gate, cause ringing\nindeed at the analog output.\nThe size of it depends heav-\nily on the values of the bond\nwire inductances. The larger\nthe inductances, the larger\nthe ringing.\nThey have to be short-\nened, or replaced by flip-\nchip bonding, as will be\nshown later.\nA more elaborate analysis\nof ground bounce is given in\nBadaroglu, JSSC July 2004,\n1119–1130.",
